      "writtenOn": "2025-06-03T10:39:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So this is called on the back of an HVC from the host, which is good, but what prevents a malicious host from not issuing that HVC?\n\nIt feels like kvm_guest_ffa_handler() should check whether that has been called before allowing FF-A requests to go through? Is this already implemented somehow and I missed it?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1600,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 1600,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "35edafc197637175fcb2f23cefd3624cea80a902",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
